# ROS 2 / colcon build artifacts (generated inside the container)
ros2_ws/build/
ros2_ws/install/
ros2_ws/log/

# Python bytecode (the perception packages are plain Python)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Recorded rosbags are NEVER stored in this repo (5.4 GB+). They live on the
# fusion-lab bench and are bind-mounted in read-only; only the replay-drive
# capability lives here. See CLAUDE.md, "Bag-driven offline perception".
*.db3
ros2_ws/**/bags/

# Model weights. YOLO weights are baked into the image at /opt/models/yolov8n.pt
# so replay is offline and reproducible; ultralytics also drops a copy into the
# CWD on first use, which must never be committed.
*.pt

# Trained gesture classifier (Phase 11). 90 MB: a 300-tree, unlimited-depth
# RandomForest, which is two orders of magnitude past the "small, code-adjacent"
# test that keeps go2_calib.npz (2 kB) in the repo. It lives on the bench and is
# bind-mounted in with ros2_ws, exactly like the rosbags and the YOLO weights.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, on purpose: the model does NOT travel with a clone. A fresh
# checkout gets the code and a loud error from load_model() pointing at
# ros2_ws/src/gesture_lab/model/README.md, not a silent wrong answer.
*.pkl

# Rendered perception replays (annotated PNGs + mp4, ~100 MB per run). Fully
# reproducible from the bag via `ros2 run fusion_lab visualize_replay.py`, so
# they are artifacts, not source. The few showcase stills used by README are
# committed under docs/images/ instead.
outputs/

# Editor / OS cruft
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Claude.MD

# Real-Jetson captures (bags + harvested dumps, ~5.8 GB) and the harvesting
# scripts that produced them. Evidence base for docs/; lives on the bench.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash — these mean the REPO-ROOT captures/ and
# scripts/ only. Unanchored, `scripts/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, which silently swallowed ros2_ws/src/gesture_lab/scripts/run_gesture.py
# (it never reached commit c393e86) and would do the same to any new file under
# fusion_lab/scripts/ — those two are tracked only because they predate this
# rule, and git keeps ignoring rules from applying to already-tracked files.
/captures/
/scripts/